---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Astra Militarum Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to the Astra Militarum? Learn how the Imperial Guard plays, which regiment to choose, how to paint infantry fast, and what to buy first."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">🪖</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Astra Militarum</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            Ordinary humans. No gene-mods, no power armor, no psychic gifts. 
            Just a lasgun, a flak vest, and orders to hold the line against things 
            that would make a Space Marine hesitate. The bravest faction in the game — 
            and the one with the best tanks.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Gunline + Armor</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium*</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$160–$230</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-3 italic">*Infantry is detail-heavy. Tanks are fast and forgiving. A mixed list is the sweet spot for new painters.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Astra Militarum?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          The Imperium of Man spans a million worlds. Defending it requires an army 
          so large that the number is effectively meaningless — billions of soldiers, 
          hundreds of thousands of tanks, artillery that can flatten cities from the horizon. 
          That army is the Astra Militarum, and every soldier in it is completely, 
          utterly ordinary.
        </p>
        <p>
          No gene-seed. No power armor. No centuries of combat experience. 
          A Guardsman is recruited from whatever world they're raised on, 
          given basic training, issued a lasgun that fires bolts of focused light, 
          and shipped to whatever warzone the Imperium needs filled with bodies. 
          Their life expectancy in active combat is measured in days.
        </p>
        <p>
          They know this. And they go anyway.
        </p>
        <p>
          That's what makes the Astra Militarum compelling in a way no other faction quite matches. 
          The Space Marines are superhuman. The Necrons are immortal machines. 
          The Astra Militarum are <em>people</em> — afraid, mortal, outnumbered — 
          and they hold the line because someone has to. 
          The Imperium does not survive without them. Every other faction in this game 
          is powerful. The Guard is brave.
        </p>
        <p>
          They compensate for individual fragility with overwhelming collective firepower, 
          armored vehicles, and artillery that can reach across entire battlefields. 
          Leman Russ battle tanks. Chimera transports. Basilisk artillery pieces 
          that lob shells twelve kilometers. When the Guard advances, it advances as a wall of steel and fire.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Regiments -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">Choose your regiment</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        The Guard draws regiments from across the Imperium — each world produces soldiers 
        shaped by their environment. Your regiment determines your colors and your army's special character.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        {[
          {
            name: 'Cadian Shock Troops',
            colors: 'Olive Green & Khaki',
            swatch: 'bg-[#4a5e3a]',
            painting: 'Easy',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: 'The default Guard regiment and GW\'s poster children. Cadians are disciplined, professional soldiers — the closest thing the Guard has to an elite core. Tan/khaki fatigues and green armor plates. Most tutorials are written for Cadian colors.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Catachan Jungle Fighters',
            colors: 'Khaki & Skin',
            swatch: 'bg-amber-700',
            painting: 'Easy',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: 'Raised on the most lethal death world in the Imperium — a planet where everything wants to kill you. Catachans are massive, bare-armed, and dressed for the jungle. Easy to paint: tan and skin tones with Agrax Earthshade does most of the work.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Valhallan Ice Warriors',
            colors: 'Grey & White',
            swatch: 'bg-slate-400',
            painting: 'Medium',
            paintColor: 'text-yellow-400',
            desc: 'Stoic survivors of a frozen death world who lost their planet to Tyranids and kept fighting anyway. Cold grey and white winter camo. Stubborn defenders with high morale in rules.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Tallarn Desert Raiders',
            colors: 'Sand & Brown',
            swatch: 'bg-yellow-700',
            painting: 'Easy',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: 'Desert warriors from a world rebuilt after an ancient war. Flowing robes, desert camo. Very fast cavalry-focused regiment. Sandy tones paint quickly with contrast paints.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Custom Regiment',
            colors: 'Your choice',
            swatch: 'bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-800 to-red-800',
            painting: 'Varies',
            paintColor: 'text-[#8a8590]',
            desc: 'Create your own homeworld, your own colors, your own backstory. The Guard supports custom regiments fully in the rules. Many players build their own with unique paint schemes.',
          },
        ].map(reg => (
          <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class={`w-4 min-h-[48px] rounded flex-shrink-0 ${reg.swatch}`}></div>
              <div class="flex-1">
                <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-3 mb-1">
                  <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg">{reg.name}</h3>
                  <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">{reg.colors}</span>
                  <span class={`text-xs font-semibold ${reg.paintColor}`}>Painting: {reg.painting}</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">{reg.desc}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          The Guard plays a <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">combined arms gunline</strong>. 
          Infantry squads hold objectives and put out volume fire. 
          Tanks push forward or sit back and delete threats. 
          Commanders issue <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Orders</strong> — special commands 
          that make nearby units shoot twice, reroll hits, hold steady, or advance and fire. 
          Every turn, your command structure is as important as your models.
        </p>
        <p>
          The cardinal rule of Guard play: 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">do not get into melee</strong>. 
          A Guardsman in hand-to-hand combat with almost anything is a dead Guardsman. 
          Your job is to keep distance, maximize firepower, and use tanks to threaten 
          anything that gets close. The Guard wins by controlling the board with fire, 
          not by fighting over ground.
        </p>
        <p>
          There are two broad approaches. 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Infantry heavy</strong> armies flood the table 
          with Guardsmen — cheap, expendable, surprisingly resilient in numbers. 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Armored Company</strong> lists go wall-to-wall tanks — 
          three or four Leman Russ variants, a Baneblade superheavy, artillery. 
          Both are completely valid, and most players land somewhere in between.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Guard are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You want real tanks on the table</li>
            <li>✓ The "ordinary humans vs. gods" story resonates</li>
            <li>✓ You like commanding an army, not a warband</li>
            <li>✓ You want overwhelming firepower and artillery</li>
            <li>✓ You love historical military aesthetics</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You don't want to assemble 40+ infantry models</li>
            <li>✗ You want your individual models to be tough</li>
            <li>✗ You want melee combat as a real option</li>
            <li>✗ You want psychic powers or alien aesthetics</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Astra Militarum</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-4 text-lg">
        The honest word: infantry squads take time. There's no getting around the detail on a Guardsman. 
        But contrast paints changed this significantly — here's the fastest method that still looks great.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] mb-10 leading-relaxed">
        We're painting Cadians. The approach transfers to any regiment — just swap the fatigue and armor colors.
      </p>

      <!-- Infantry -->
      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold mb-4 text-[#f0ede8]">Infantry (Cadian Shock Troops)</h3>
      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Spray Zandri Dust</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A warm tan base coat that becomes the fatigues and clothing. The armor plates will be painted green on top of this.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Militarum Green Contrast on all armor plates</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">The jacket, trousers, straps, and pouches. One coat. The contrast paint shades itself into folds and creases.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Leave fatigues and clothing as Zandri Dust, wash with Agrax Earthshade</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">The shoulder pads, helmet, and chest armor stay the base tan color. One wash of Agrax over the whole model ties everything together and adds instant grime.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Leadbelcher on the lasgun</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Metal on the barrel and body. Black on the stock. Quick and effective.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Kislev Flesh on skin, base the model</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Face and hands. A thin layer of Kislev Flesh, maybe a light shade of Reikland Fleshshade. Then base with a sandy texture paint and a tuft.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Tanks -->
      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold mb-4 text-[#f0ede8]">Tanks (Leman Russ & vehicles)</h3>
      <div class="space-y-4 mb-8">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Spray Zandri Dust, then heavy drybrush Ushabti Bone</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Covers the hull. The drybrush over the spray creates a natural worn look before you've done anything else.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Agrax Earthshade wash over the whole vehicle</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Flows into panel lines and rivets. Tanks have a lot of rivets. The wash does all the work of making them read as detail.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Leadbelcher on tracks, barrels, and metal trim</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Drybrush along the track links and stipple it onto barrel tips and exhaust vents.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Ryza Rust on track edges, Nuln Oil on recesses</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Optional but very effective. Drybrush Ryza Rust on the track edges for battle damage. Everything looks like it's been in a warzone without any skill required.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">The real talk on infantry</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Infantry squads take longer than Necrons or Orks. A 10-man squad 
          done properly with contrast paints takes about 2–3 hours. 
          That's fine — batch paint them in groups of 10, do one step across all 10 before moving on, 
          and you'll have a squad done in a session. 
          The tanks are the reward: one Leman Russ painted to a great standard in an hour is deeply satisfying.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">Start with the Combat Patrol. It gives you infantry AND a vehicle — the right introduction to how the army actually works.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Astra Militarum</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Includes Cadian Shock Troops (your core infantry), a Chimera APC (transport vehicle and fire support), 
          a Company Commander (issues orders), and a Heavy Weapons Squad (crew-served weapons). 
          A legal, playable force that covers all the roles the army needs.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.games-workshop.com/en-US/Astra-Militarum-Combat-Patrol"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Buy from Games Workshop →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$65 · the obvious second purchase</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Leman Russ Battle Tank</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          The iconic Guard tank. One kit builds multiple variants — 
          Battle Cannon for general use, Demolisher Cannon for close-range destruction, 
          Exterminator for anti-infantry. Adds serious firepower and is one of the most 
          satisfying models to paint in the entire game.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.games-workshop.com/en-US/Leman-Russ-Battle-Tank"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          View on Games Workshop →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need (Cadian scheme)</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Zandri Dust Spray', use: 'Base coat — infantry armor and vehicle hull', required: true },
            { name: 'Militarum Green (Contrast)', use: 'Fatigues, webbing, straps', required: true },
            { name: 'Agrax Earthshade', use: 'Full model wash — grime and shadow', required: true },
            { name: 'Leadbelcher', use: 'Guns, tracks, metal fittings', required: true },
            { name: 'Kislev Flesh', use: 'Skin on faces and hands', required: true },
            { name: 'Ushabti Bone', use: 'Drybrush highlight on armor and hull', required: false },
            { name: 'Ryza Rust', use: 'Battle damage on tracks and edges', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">~$38 for the full set. The same paints work across your entire army — infantry and vehicles both.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: 'Combat Patrol: Astra Militarum', cost: '~$160', note: 'Infantry, Chimera, Commander, Heavy Weapons' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (5)', cost: '~$38', note: 'Spray + contrast + wash + metal + flesh' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Sandy texture paint + tufts' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Superglue', cost: '~$5', note: 'Multi-part infantry kits' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$235</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        The Leman Russ (~$65) is the natural next purchase and worth budgeting for early. 
        A Guardsman army without a tank feels incomplete — and the tank is the most fun thing to paint.
      </p>
